All 15 tests pass (`pytest -q` → `15 passed in 0.02s`). Only `src/` was touched; no changes to `tests/`, no skips/xfails added.

Five bugs fixed across three modules:

- **`src/auth.py`** — `has_permission` now compares roles case-insensitively (`role.lower() == required.lower()`); `is_admin_or_owner` now uses `or` (admin alone or owner alone grants access), matching its docstring and tests.
- **`src/inventory.py`** — `__init__` copies `initial` instead of binding a shared mutable default; `add` accumulates (`stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`); `reserve` only raises `OutOfStock` when `qty > available` (reserving exactly available is allowed); `release` raises `ValueError` when releasing more than reserved.
- **`src/text_utils.py`** — `slugify` lowercases and collapses runs of separators down to one `-`; `truncate` reserves `len(suffix)` characters so the result fits within `max_len` (with a guard for `max_len <= len(suffix)`).
